<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67387" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μήλιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μάλ</span></b> - <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			5(1).1
		</span></i><i><span class="en">
			<u>B</u>
			1
		</span></i> (Sparta, <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
			12(3).1097
		</span></i>, al. (<span class="entity">Melos</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from the island of Meios,
			Melian</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				672
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.91
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμὸς</span> M., prov. of
			famine, because of the extremities to which the island was reduced
			at its siege, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				186
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Μηλία</span>, with or without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>, <i>a greyish aluminous earth</i>,
			which painters mixed with mineral colours, to give them consistency, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.159
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
